## Why This Is Asked

Explores privacy-preserving design, cross-geo data handling, and realistic testing strategies in real-time analytics.

## Key Concepts

- Privacy-preserving ID mapping and masking
- Immutable audit/logging for compliance
- Synthetic data generation with deterministic seeds
- Correctness under backpressure, partition rebalancing, and clock skew
- Data lineage and access controls across geographies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: map PII to surrogate for privacy
function toSurrogate(userId, pii) {
  const surrogateId = hash(userId + 'salt');
  const maskedPii = mask(pii);
  return { surrogateId, maskedPii };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify determinism of surrogate IDs across partitions and runs?
- How would you perform backfill tests with synthetic data while preserving audit integrity?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design offline-first features, idempotency, and conflict handling for mobile apps. Challenges include eventual consistency, sync retries, and safe canary rollout.

## Key Concepts
- Offline-first architecture
- Idempotent API design and deduplication
- Conflict resolution with timestamped records
- Data model versioning and canary controls
- Local testing strategies for offline/sync workflows

## Code Example
```javascript
function mergeScore(local, incoming) {
  // last write wins by client_timestamp per user
  if (incoming.client_timestamp > local.client_timestamp) {
    return { ...local, ...incoming };
  }
  return local;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test offline queue size and eviction policy?
- How would you handle partial failures during batch sync?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a robust ingestion and auditing path for a privacy-preserving cca_score with revocation.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotent ingestion and exactly-once processing
- Versioned, tamper-evident ledger and revocation/delta application
- Streaming pipelines and baseline vs. incremental recomputation
- Cryptographic signing and cross-tenant isolation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example signature verification
function verifyShareSignature(share, publicKey) {
  const { payload, signature } = share;
  // verify using chosen crypto (Ed25519/ECDSA)
  return crypto.verify(publicKey, payload, signature);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test revocation at scale (latency, integrity)?
- How would you enforce per-tenant data isolation in a shared ledger?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluate ability to design safe multi-region rollout with deterministic routing and robust rollback mechanisms.

## Key Concepts
- Deterministic routing via consistent hashing
- Region-aware feature weighting and versioning
- Comprehensive observability and rollback criteria
- Data-plane safety and auditability

## Code Example
```javascript
// JavaScript example: deterministic bucketing by user_id
function bucket(userId, buckets) {
  let h = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < userId.length; i++) h = (h * 31 + userId.charCodeAt(i)) >>> 0;
  return h % buckets;
}
```

